# LoopBack testing (read only)

Use this when checking live inventory data, PR / batch / expiry behavior, or any API-backed test.

- Base URL is `API_BASE_URL` in `public/config.js` (verified: `https://zenthtrain.beautecloud.com/lb/api`).
- GET does not need an `Authorization` token. A filter query works, for example `ItemBatches?filter={"limit":1}`.
- Read only. Do not POST, PUT, PATCH, or DELETE unless the user explicitly asks for a write in that turn.
- `ItemBatches` on this database has both empty-batch rows (`batchNo` blank, `expDate` null) and real batches with expiry. HQ sample: item `11600277`, site `ZEHQ`, batch `A01`, UOM `PIECE`, expiry `2025-12-25`.

PR with batch and expiry on: the outlet does not pick a batch. The line is saved as `fefo-<UOM>`. HQ assigns a specific batch only in approval mode. Automatic stock posting (`executePrTransferPost`, one-way approval, Delivery Order Out) throws when `BATCH_NO` is `Yes`. The path that applies batch and expiry is an open transfer posted from the GTI screen.
